                <pb facs="0808" n="710" sameAs="frus:frus1920v01/pg710"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77/1717a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Crane</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-09-18T18:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 18,
                                1920—6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>239. Reports are current that China has sent a note to Japan making a protest
                    against Japanese soldiers being quartered along Chinese Eastern line. Can you
                    verify these reports? If possible, send early reply.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Colby</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
